Tell a hosted plugin of the older format its display scale before it opens.

JUCE sends the scale to a plugin that declares supportsViewDpiScaling through
effVendorSpecific('PreS', 'AeCs'), but nativeScaleFactor is written only by
NativeScaleFactorNotifier, which reports through MessageManager::callAsync.
openPluginWindow() therefore sends 1.0 right before effEditOpen, and the real
factor arrives a message loop after the editor was built. DPF reads the scale
once, while constructing its UI, so its plugins drew at half size on a 200%
display for the life of the window. The fix reads the peer's scale before
opening — the twin of juce-vst3-scale-before-attach.patch for VST3.
diff --git a/modules/juce_audio_processors/format_types/juce_VSTPluginFormat.cpp b/modules/juce_audio_processors/format_types/juce_VSTPluginFormat.cpp
index 8c175221c..914ed3283 100644
--- a/modules/juce_audio_processors/format_types/juce_VSTPluginFormat.cpp
+++ b/modules/juce_audio_processors/format_types/juce_VSTPluginFormat.cpp
@@ -401,6 +401,17 @@ private:
 
         pluginRespondsToDPIChanges = plugin.pluginCanDo ("supportsViewDpiScaling") > 0;
 
+        // PLECTRIFY_VST2_SCALE_BEFORE_OPEN: take the display scale straight from
+        // the peer before effEditOpen, for plugins that read it only while
+        // building their UI. nativeScaleFactor is otherwise written by
+        // NativeScaleFactorNotifier alone, which reports through callAsync and
+        // so lands a message loop after the editor has opened against the 1.0
+        // placeholder; DPF and other frameworks that apply the scale once then
+        // draw at 1:1 for the life of the window. Same fix as the VST3 one
+        // (juce-vst3-scale-before-attach.patch).
+        if (auto* peer = getTopLevelComponent()->getPeer())
+            nativeScaleFactor = (float) peer->getPlatformScaleFactor();
+
         setContentScaleFactor();
 
         Vst2::ERect* rect = nullptr;
